    {
      "text": "On local solutions of the Ramanujan equation and their connection formulae — We show connection formulae of local solutions of the Ramanujan equation between the origin and the inﬁnity.\n\n**On local solutions of the Ramanujan equation and their connection formulae**\n\n*Takeshi MORITA∗*\n\n19 pp, 14 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We show connection formulae of local solutions of the Ramanujan equation between the origin and the inﬁnity. These solutions are given by the Ramanujan function, the q-Airy function and the divergent basic hypergeometric series 2ϕ0(0, 0; −; q, x). We use two diﬀerent q- Borel-Laplace transformations to obtain our connection formulae.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Basic notations; 3 Two types of the q-analogue of the Airy func; 3.1 The Ramanujan function Aq(x); 3.2 The q-Airy function Aiq(x); 3.3 Covering transformations; 3.4 The q-Airy equation around the infinity; 3.5 The q-Borel transformation and the q-Lapla; 3.6 The connection formula of the q-Airy funct; 4 Connection formula of the divergent series 2; 4.1 Two different q-exponential functions; 4.2 The connection formula and alternate repre; 4.3 The connection formula of the series 20(0,",
